## Summary
An article reports that 81.7% of integrated care personnel are juggling additional tasks such as issuing certified copies and processing civil complaints alongside their primary duties, leading to an overwhelming workload that hampers their ability to provide integrated care services.

## Key Points
- 81.7% of integrated care personnel are involved in dual jobs or concurrent tasks.
- Administrative duties like issuing certified copies and civil complaint processing are cited as burdensome.
- The overload of tasks affects the effectiveness and quality of integrated care services.
- There is a systemic issue in workload distribution for healthcare or social care workers.
- The situation highlights the need for policy or operational improvements to support integrated care personnel.


